infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Protobuf vs JSON: the honest numbers
  desc Raw size lead shrinks under gzip — parse cost and typed stubs are the durable wins
  compares
    - label Protobuf (binary, tag-keyed)
      children
        - label 2-5x smaller raw
          desc Tagged binary vs text, before any compression
        - label 5-10x faster to parse
          desc Arithmetic on varint keys, not text scanning
        - label Tags 1-15 cost 1 byte
          desc Hot fields earn small numbers; 16-2047 cost 2 bytes
        - label Typed generated stubs
          desc Compiler enforces the contract — no json.RawMessage archaeology
    - label JSON (text)
      children
        - label Only 1.5-2x larger gzipped
          desc gzip eats most of protobuf's raw size advantage
        - label Human-readable
          desc Debuggable by eye, no codegen step
        - label Text scanning to parse
          desc Slower decode, more allocations on the hot path
        - label Drifts in documentation
          desc No compiled contract — both ends can silently disagree
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
